# hyp: merge shapes for the files the plugin's hooks and writers touch (written by /hyp:init;
# re-running init adds any missing row and never removes yours).
#
# Append-only row files -- one self-contained JSON object per line, newline-terminated, each row
# carrying its own date, so file order never matters and a union merge (both branches' rows kept,
# no line-position dependence) is a valid ledger. Never edit a landed row in place.
{{LEDGER_FILE}} merge=union
{{OM_FEEDBACK_FILE}} merge=union
{{OM_SUBSTRATES_FILE}} merge=union
{{ROUTING_LEDGER_FILE}} merge=union
.claude/leak-meter-fires.log merge=union
#
# Compiled projections -- regenerated whole from their sources, never merged line by line
# (merge=binary: git writes no conflict markers into them). When a merge stops on one of them:
#   python3 "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/compile-dashboard.py" <root>
#   git add DASHBOARD.md decisions.html
#   git commit --no-edit
# and when it stops on a north-star page (ledger/north-stars/*.html):
#   python3 "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/compile-north-star-progress.py" --all --repo <root>
#   git add ledger/north-stars
#   git commit --no-edit
DASHBOARD.md merge=binary -diff linguist-generated
decisions.html merge=binary -diff linguist-generated
ledger/north-stars/*.html merge=binary -diff linguist-generated
